00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:01.790
Abraham: Hi I’m Abraham

00:00:01.970 --> 00:00:02.890
Nicole: and I’m Nicole

00:00:03.250 --> 00:00:05.920
and throughout this course we
will be talking to you about

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:07.960
different aspects of cyber security

00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:12.630
Abraham: In these introductory videos we
will look at the concept of cyber security

00:00:12.670 --> 00:00:14.250
and why it is important everywhere.

00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:19.509
The core function of cyber security is
to protect our systems, networks and

00:00:19.509 --> 00:00:24.630
devices and the services we access both
online and in our place of work, keeping

00:00:24.630 --> 00:00:29.260
them safe from digital surveillance,
theft, or damage, known as cybercrime.

00:00:29.770 --> 00:00:33.440
Nicole: The use of new technologies
and the internet has given criminals

00:00:33.469 --> 00:00:37.519
a new tool for committing crime
which can subsequently take place

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:39.550
'virtually' anywhere in the world.

00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:44.070
Cyber crime is increasing all the
time and is becoming more complex

00:00:44.099 --> 00:00:48.540
affecting essential services,
companies and individuals whilst

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:50.459
also threatening national security.

00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:54.820
So why is cyber security so important?

00:00:55.620 --> 00:00:59.480
Abraham: Nearly everything we do today
involves using smart phones, computers

00:00:59.590 --> 00:01:03.440
and the internet and it’s hard to
see how we can function without them.

00:01:04.379 --> 00:01:09.109
Online banking, shopping, ordering
an Uber or a pizza, we put our

00:01:09.110 --> 00:01:12.780
information out there hoping it is
safe from cyber criminals that may

00:01:12.809 --> 00:01:14.710
use it for their nefarious activities!

00:01:15.270 --> 00:01:16.979
But how can you be sure it is safe?

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:20.060
Nicole: Just think about this for
a minute, would you leave your

00:01:20.060 --> 00:01:23.629
most valuable possessions on show
for anyone to see or pick up?

00:01:24.179 --> 00:01:25.770
Well, it is the same for your data!

00:01:26.259 --> 00:01:29.960
We are all at risk of having our
personal information stolen by cyber

00:01:29.960 --> 00:01:34.680
criminals to sell on to others, create
false identities, or to use it to con

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:36.490
us into giving out more information.

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:40.700
So what are the key
concepts of Cyber security?

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:47.949
Abraham:
Confidentiality…Integrity…Availability…Authentication.

00:01:50.220 --> 00:01:55.630
Confidentiality means controlling access
levels of data and sensitive information.

00:01:55.970 --> 00:02:00.669
It should only be available to those who
have right to view, store or transmit

00:02:00.710 --> 00:02:04.819
it, and if someone doesn’t need to
know, then they shouldn’t have access.

00:02:05.330 --> 00:02:08.232
Integrity means that all information
is maintained safely as it

00:02:08.410 --> 00:02:10.060
should be with no modifications.

00:02:10.620 --> 00:02:14.450
Sensitive data should not be tampered
with or compromised by any means.

00:02:15.270 --> 00:02:19.930
Nicole: Availability means that sensitive
information and data should not be readily

00:02:19.930 --> 00:02:24.219
available but should be accessible to
those who have the appropriate authority

00:02:24.260 --> 00:02:25.720
at a time the time they need it.

00:02:26.090 --> 00:02:29.460
Abraham: Authentication- means controls
need to be in place to authenticate

00:02:29.480 --> 00:02:33.890
the identity of users and that access
is given to the appropriate people.

00:02:34.550 --> 00:02:38.890
To help to make this more secure
multifactor authentication should be used.

00:02:39.809 --> 00:02:43.059
Nicole: We often talk about
risk but what is risk?

00:02:43.350 --> 00:02:46.430
In simple terms risk means
something bad happening.

00:02:46.790 --> 00:02:51.170
In terms of cyber security, risk
is the potential for loss, damage

00:02:51.250 --> 00:02:53.330
or destruction of assets or data.

00:02:54.030 --> 00:02:58.169
Risk can be affected by a vulnerability,
which is a weakness that can create

00:02:58.209 --> 00:03:00.280
exposure to a threat or a hazard.

00:03:00.930 --> 00:03:04.160
Having adequate cyber security
can help can minimise that risk.

00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:06.920
Abraham: Hazards are the
probability of an occurrence of

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:08.470
something potentially damaging.

00:03:09.030 --> 00:03:12.390
Threats show more intent and
are more likely to harm and

00:03:12.390 --> 00:03:15.769
vulnerability is how susceptible
you are to that hazard or threat.

00:03:16.789 --> 00:03:21.050
Nicole: So, there you are the basic
concept of cyber security, but don’t

00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:24.790
worry if it seems a bit confusing,
as you progress through this course

00:03:24.830 --> 00:03:28.580
you will look at these and other
terms in more detail and get a full

00:03:28.580 --> 00:03:30.920
understanding of Cyber Security practices.

